{"path":"string/wide/iswdigit","title":"iswdigit","titleHtml":"iswdigit","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/string/wide/iswdigit","section":"string","kind":"page","summary":"Checks if the given wide character corresponds (if narrowed) to one of the ten decimal digit characters 0123456789.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/c/string/wide\"><code>&lt;wctype.h&gt;</code></a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">int</span> iswdigit<span class=\"br0\">(</span> wint_t ch <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c95\">(since C95)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Checks if the given wide character corresponds (if narrowed) to one of the ten decimal digit characters <span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"nu19\">0123456789</span></span>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> ch\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> wide character\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>Non-zero value if the wide character is a numeric character, zero otherwise.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p><code>iswdigit</code> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/c/string/wide/iswxdigit\">iswxdigit</a></span> are the only standard wide character classification functions that are not affected by the currently installed C locale.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\"><p>Some locales offer additional character classes that detect non-ASCII digits</p>\n<pre data-lang=\"c\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;locale.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include 